<p>The final and most critical layer of safety involves high-tensile ratchet lashing systems. These straps, woven from synthetic fibers with steel-core reinforcements, are tightened to precise tension specifications using calibrated ratchet handles. This technique eliminates slack, ensuring that the vehicle is firmly anchored to the carrier’s anchor points.</p>
<p>The high-tensile nature of the ratchets prevents stretching over time, maintaining constant pressure even during prolonged highway transit. This rigorous protocol is why top-tier car delivery service providers prioritize ratchet lashing over simple tie-downs, as it effectively neutralizes the effects of centrifugal force during sharp turns and aerodynamic lift at high speeds.</p>
